WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:15.708
"And then Athena started yelling at Aphrodite."

2
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:18.649
Brody's voice was shaky as he told his story.

3
00:00:18.669 --> 00:00:22.550
"I just put on my old chiton and sandals and got out of there."

4
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.671
Julia had always seen Brody looking cocky and confident.

5
00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:30.572
But right now he seemed upset and unsure of himself.

6
00:00:31.648 --> 00:00:35.792
He'd come rushing out of the bath ten minutes earlier, babbling about almost being poisoned.

7
00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:41.597
She and Markos had led him to a private spot outside the gymnasium, where he'd told them the

8
00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:43.518
whole story of Aphrodite's visit.

9
00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:47.282
"Wow," Julia said.

10
00:00:47.302 --> 00:00:50.324
"And Athena mentioned Zeus' wife, Hera?"

11
00:00:50.344 --> 00:00:52.906
"Yeah," Brody said.

12
00:00:52.926 --> 00:00:57.070
"She seemed to think Aphrodite and Hera were working together or something."

13
00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:02.431
"That makes sense," Julia said, thinking back on the Greek myths she'd read.

14
00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:06.114
"I mean, it sounds like something Hera might do.

15
00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.436
It reminds me of the story about the Shirt of Nessus."

16
00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:11.378
"The shirt of what?"

17
00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.799
Brody looked blank.

18
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.843
"Never mind, I'll tell you about it some other time," Julia said.

19
00:01:17.863 --> 00:01:20.646
"But what about trying to escape?

20
00:01:21.026 --> 00:01:21.827
Are you ready now?"

21
00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:24.389
Brody thought for a second.

22
00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:26.631
"Maybe," he said.

23
00:01:26.651 --> 00:01:27.772
"But how?"

24
00:01:29.012 --> 00:01:32.193
"We need to find a way to sneak into the Temple of Caerus."

25
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:34.193
Julia glanced at Markos.

26
00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:35.814
"Will you help us?"

27
00:01:36.994 --> 00:01:38.535
She expected him to say no.

28
00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:42.556
To her surprise, however, Markos looked thoughtful.

29
00:01:42.576 --> 00:01:48.117
"Did Athena truly say that Hera and Aphrodite were working together?"

30
00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:49.117
he asked.

31
00:01:49.137 --> 00:01:52.418
"Because that would be quite unusual."

32
00:01:52.438 --> 00:01:54.999
"Why?" Brody said.

33
00:01:55.019 --> 00:01:58.460
"Wouldn't anyone want to work with Aphrodite?"

34
00:01:59.412 --> 00:02:01.273
Julia looked at him in astonishment.

35
00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.274
"She just tried to kill you, dummy!

36
00:02:04.514 --> 00:02:06.215
You can't still have a crush on her!"

37
00:02:07.316 --> 00:02:09.277
Looking unhappy, Brody shrugged.

38
00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:11.878
Markos looked troubled now.

39
00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:18.161
"Both Hermes and my father have ordered me to keep you safe," he told Brody.

40
00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:23.163
"But if Hera is after you, there is no safety for you in Olympia.

41
00:02:23.563 --> 00:02:25.244
Or anywhere in Greece, for that matter.

42
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.023
Once Hera develops a grudge against someone, she won't stop until she's destroyed him."

43
00:02:30.823 --> 00:02:31.523
He shuddered.

44
00:02:31.543 --> 00:02:34.405
"Even Zeus himself is not always safe."

45
00:02:34.425 --> 00:02:38.647
"That's why we need to get home," Julia said.

46
00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.608
"Back to our own time."

47
00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:42.850
She looked at Markos.

48
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.310
Would he help them?

49
00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.552
Or would he tell Hermes what they were planning?

50
00:02:49.653 --> 00:02:53.976
She and Brody had told Markos about the time passage in the temple on their first night in

51
00:02:54.016 --> 00:02:58.177
Greece. But Markos hadn't said much in response.

52
00:02:59.018 --> 00:03:01.879
Julia wasn't sure he believed they'd really come from the future.

53
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.341
Finally Markos nodded.

54
00:03:04.361 --> 00:03:07.162
"I will try to help," he said.

55
00:03:07.182 --> 00:03:12.726
"In return, I ask only that you not tell Hermes that I did so.

56
00:03:13.966 --> 00:03:18.229
If he learns of my help, he will be angry and could even take out that anger on

57
00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:20.450
my father or the rest of my family."

58
00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.572
"Don't worry," Julia said.

59
00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:27.698
"Once we get out of here, we're planning never to see Hermes again.

60
00:03:28.138 --> 00:03:33.061
Now listen, I've been thinking about this, and I have some ideas about how we could get away.

61
00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:37.624
The three of them spent the rest of the day concocting their plan.

62
00:03:40.226 --> 00:03:42.867
By dinnertime Julia was feeling confident.

63
00:03:44.368 --> 00:03:49.371
Hermes and Caerus entered the courtyard and took their seats at the table, just as they'd done the

64
00:03:49.471 --> 00:03:50.132
evening before.

65
00:03:51.572 --> 00:03:56.413
Julia watched from the doorway as Hermes started talking to Brody about his plans for training.

66
00:03:57.574 --> 00:04:00.735
Finally he turned away to talk with Markos' father.

67
00:04:01.855 --> 00:04:05.536
Julia hurried over to serve Brody a second helping of grilled fish.

68
00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:08.357
"You know what to do, right?"

69
00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:13.438
she whispered, glad for once that the girls and women of the household waited on the men and

70
00:04:13.478 --> 00:04:16.859
boys. Brody shoved some figs in his mouth.

71
00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:20.960
"You know, I'll miss some of this food," he mumbled.

72
00:04:22.416 --> 00:04:25.157
"Shh!" Julia shot a worried look at Hermes.

73
00:04:26.218 --> 00:04:32.040
But Markos' father was telling a joke, and Hermes and Caerus were chuckling and paying no attention to

74
00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:38.243
Brody. Julia thought the meal would never end.

75
00:04:39.123 --> 00:04:41.684
But at last the two gods stood up from the table.

76
00:04:41.704 --> 00:04:44.785
"We must go," Hermes announced.

77
00:04:45.606 --> 00:04:46.406
He looked at Brody.

78
00:04:46.426 --> 00:04:49.287
"Be ready early tomorrow, my champion.

79
00:04:49.728 --> 00:04:50.608
We have much to do."

80
00:04:51.808 --> 00:04:53.289
"Okay," Brody said.

81
00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.891
Julia was relieved.

82
00:04:57.112 --> 00:05:01.676
Hermes and Caerus always went to the agora to hang out with their god friends after dinner.

83
00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:06.200
She hoped they would stay away long enough for the kids' plan to work.

84
00:05:07.541 --> 00:05:11.344
"Oops!" she said, intentionally spilling water on Brody.

85
00:05:11.364 --> 00:05:14.447
"Hey!" Brody blustered.

86
00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:18.270
"Oh! I mean, um, I'd better change clothes."

87
00:05:19.811 --> 00:05:20.932
Julia glared at him.

88
00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:25.838
It was a good thing he was talented at football, because he wasn't much of an actor!

89
00:05:27.218 --> 00:05:28.839
Luckily Markos was much better.

90
00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:30.580
He turned to Julia.

91
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.061
"Fetch us a dry chiton immediately."

92
00:05:33.081 --> 00:05:36.142
"Of course," Julia said.

93
00:05:36.923 --> 00:05:37.743
She rushed off.

94
00:05:39.844 --> 00:05:42.365
Moments later all three met outside the house.

95
00:05:42.385 --> 00:05:46.247
"That was pretty slick," Brody said with a grin.

96
00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:50.224
"Do you think we convinced your family, Markos?"

97
00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:52.425
Markos cast an anxious look at the house.

98
00:05:52.445 --> 00:05:55.586
"We should hurry," he said.

99
00:05:55.606 --> 00:05:58.106
"I'll be missed if I don't return soon."

100
00:05:58.126 --> 00:06:01.847
"You don't have to come with us," Julia told him.

101
00:06:01.867 --> 00:06:05.348
"It's not as if we'll get lost on the way to the temple."

102
00:06:06.488 --> 00:06:10.970
She gestured to the pale stone building, which was glowing in the moonlight above them.

103
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.110
"We can see it from here."

104
00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.091
"It's all right," Markos said.

105
00:06:16.111 --> 00:06:19.172
"I should come along in case you run into any trouble."

106
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.861
The three of them started for the path to the temple.

107
00:06:23.961 --> 00:06:26.282
Brody was in the lead as they rounded a turn.

108
00:06:26.302 --> 00:06:29.723
"Almost there," he said over his shoulder.

109
00:06:29.743 --> 00:06:31.683
"I think there's—ah!"

110
00:06:32.823 --> 00:06:36.624
He jumped back, startled, as something burst from a bush beside the trail.

111
00:06:37.185 --> 00:06:40.005
There was a flapping of wings and a loud caw!

112
00:06:41.086 --> 00:06:42.426
Brody laughed with relief.

113
00:06:43.486 --> 00:06:45.667
"Oh, man," he said.

114
00:06:45.687 --> 00:06:47.367
"It's just a bird."

115
00:06:48.948 --> 00:06:51.501
"A raven," Markos said, smiling.

116
00:06:51.521 --> 00:06:55.482
"Let's keep moving," Julia said, pushing ahead.

117
00:06:55.502 --> 00:07:01.984
"With any luck we should be there in less than—" She gasped as a tall form stepped out

118
00:07:02.004 --> 00:07:03.345
of the shadows just ahead.

119
00:07:03.365 --> 00:07:09.187
"Good evening, young mortals," Hera said.

120
00:07:09.207 --> 00:07:11.687
"Going somewhere?"
